{"uid": "mfg-1912-13-03", "question_type": "explanatory", "question_subtype": "shortfall_cause", "raw_text": "Based on the daily ledger and events for Plant 1912, Period 13:\n\n**Day 170:** MASR025K had opening stock of 582, produced 0, ordered 687. Only 582 could ship, leaving 105 backordered and stock at 0.\n\n**Day 171:** MASR025K had opening stock of 0, produced 150. Total available: 150 units. The queue (oldest first) had 105 units of backorder from day 170, plus the new 207-unit order. The 150 units shipped: 105 to the day 170 backorder, 45 to the day 171 order. The day 171 order left 162 backordered.\n\n**Dispatch capacity on day 171:** ATN02K12P shipped 655 \u00d7 24kg = 15,720kg; MAR02K12P shipped 64 \u00d7 24kg = 1,536kg; MASR025K shipped 150 \u00d7 25kg = 3,750kg. Total: 21,006kg, well under the 34,500kg capacity limit. Capacity was NOT reached (confirmed by Events log, which notes capacity reached on days 170, 173, 175 but not 171).\n\nEvaluating each choice:\n- **Choice 0:** If production on day 170 had been \u2265687, the day 170 order would have been fulfilled, no backorder would exist, and day 171 would have had sufficient stock (582+150=732 \u2265 207) to ship the order in full. **Responsible.**\n- **Choice 1:** If there had been enough stock on day 171, the order would have shipped in full. The insufficiency of stock (150 available vs. 312 total demand) directly prevented full shipment. **Responsible.**\n- **Choice 2:** Capacity was not a constraint on day 171 (only 21,006 of 34,500 kg used). Removing ATN02K12P shipments wouldn't change the outcome. **Not responsible.**\n- **Choice 3:** Dispatch capacity was not reached on day 171. This condition did not occur. **Not responsible.**\n\n```json\n{\"choices\": {\"0\": true, \"1\": true, \"2\": false, \"3\": false}}\n```", "parsed": {"choices": {"0": true, "1": true, "2": false, "3": false}}, "score": {"question_correct": true, "options_correct": 4, "options_total": 4}, "usage": {"input_tokens": 53161,